question: how to distinguish systems that merely accumulate complexity from 
those that organize complexity in a reusable, resilient, and self-stabilizing 
manner. Recent theoretical work characterizes intelligence not as behavior 
or optimization, but as a regime of effective structural compression—systems 
that assemble complexity while increasing their capacity to reuse and 
stabilize it over time. Spherepop OS is designed to make such distinctions 
structurally explicit rather than behaviorally inferred.
