C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Parsimony, Self-Consistency, and Semantic Assembly}

Recent work on the mathematical foundations of intelligence proposes that 
intelligent systems are governed by two core principles: parsimony and 
self-consistency. Parsimony refers to the discovery of low-dimensional, 
predictive structure—compression that avoids combinatorial explosion. 
Self-consistency requires that internal representations remain stable enough 
to support simulation, counterfactual reasoning, and prediction.

Spherepop OS does not implement intelligence directly. Instead, it provides 
a deterministic semantic substrate in which these principles can be realized 
and made explicit. Parsimony corresponds, at the system level, to the emergence 
of reusable semantic structure: equivalence classes, shared subgraphs, and 
collapsed regions that amortize construction cost across contexts. 
Self-consistency is enforced by design through replay determinism, total 
causal order, and strict separation between authoritative state transitions 
and derived views.

Within this framework, memorization corresponds to unstructured growth of 
the event log—new events that do not increase reuse or abstraction. 
Abstraction corresponds to transformations that increase the future 
compressibility of semantic structure by reorganizing the assembly graph 
itself. The system thereby distinguishes raw accumulation from effective 
assembly at the level of construction history rather than external behavior.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
