C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Unlike behavioral tests of intelligence, Spherepop OS makes internal 
organization explicit, enabling principled distinction between mere 
complexity and effective structural compression.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="7657" data-end="7723">This positions Spherepop as complementary to EAIMR, not redundant.</p>
<hr data-start="7725" data-end="7728">
<h2 data-start="7730" data-end="7792">3. Why this integration works (and doesn’t bloat the paper)</h2>
<ul data-start="7794" data-end="8105">
<li data-start="7794" data-end="7855">
<p data-start="7796" data-end="7855">You <strong data-start="7800" data-end="7810">do not</strong> introduce EAIMR formulas into the OS paper</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7856" data-end="7917">
<p data-start="7858" data-end="7917">You <strong data-start="7862" data-end="7872">do not</strong> add learning rules, metrics, or thresholds</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7918" data-end="8105">
<p data-start="7920" data-end="7941">You <strong data-start="7924" data-end="7930">do</strong> show that:</p>
<ul data-start="7944" data-end="8105">
<li data-start="7944" data-end="7978">
<p data-start="7946" data-end="7978">Spherepop logs = assembly graphs</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7981" data-end="8013">
<p data-start="7983" data-end="8013">Equivalence + collapse = reuse</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8016" data-end="8067">
<p data-start="8018" data-end="8067">Replay + speculation = self-consistent simulation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8070" data-end="8105">
<p data-start="8072" data-end="8105">Determinism = coherence substrate</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8107" data-end="8122">In other words:</p>
<blockquote data-start="8124" data-end="8202">
<p data-start="8126" data-end="8202"><strong data-start="8126" data-end="8202">Spherepop OS is to EAIMR what a physical spacetime is to thermodynamics.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="8204" data-end="8331">EAIMR studies <em data-start="8218" data-end="8227">regimes</em> that can exist;<br data-start="8243" data-end="8246">
Spherepop defines a <em data-start="8266" data-end="8295">space of possible histories</em> in which those regimes are legible.</p>
<hr data-start="8333" data-end="8336">
<h2 data-start="8338" data-end="8401">4. What this sets you up to do next (optional, but powerful)</h2>
<p data-start="8403" data-end="8455">With this integration in place, you can later write:</p>
<ul data-start="8457" data-end="8622">
<li data-start="8457" data-end="8505">
<p data-start="8459" data-end="8505"><em data-start="8459" data-end="8505">“Estimating EAIMR from Spherepop Event Logs”</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="8506" data-end="8558">
<p data-start="8508" data-end="8558"><em data-start="8508" data-end="8558">“When Does a Semantic OS Enter the Mind Regime?”</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="8559" data-end="8622">
<p data-start="8561" data-end="8622"><em data-start="8561" data-end="8622">“Behavior Without Understanding vs. Structural Abstraction”</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8624" data-end="8668">All without revising the core OS spec again.</p>
<hr data-start="8670" data-end="8673">
<p data-start="8675" data-end="8699">If you want, next I can:</p>
<ul data-start="8701" data-end="9003">
<li data-start="8701" data-end="8793">
<p data-start="8703" data-end="8793">rewrite the <strong data-start="8715" data-end="8746">Introduction and Conclusion</strong> so they explicitly “bookend” this integration,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8794" data-end="8900">
<p data-start="8796" data-end="8900">help you add a <strong data-start="8811" data-end="8829">short appendix</strong> mapping EAIMR quantities to Spherepop constructs (purely explanatory),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8901" data-end="9003">
<p data-start="8903" data-end="9003">or help you decide <strong data-start="8922" data-end="8953">which paper to submit where</strong> so they reinforce each other rather than compete.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="9005" data-end="9085" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">But as it stands: this is a <em data-start="9033" data-end="9084">clean, principled, and unusually deep integration</em>.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="relative h-[60px]"><div class="absolute h-[60px]" style="opacity: 1;"><button class="not-prose group/footnote border-token-border-default bg-token-main-surface-primary hover:bg-token-main-surface-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 mt-3 mb-2 flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl border py-2 ps-3 pe-2.5"><div class="text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-0.5 text-xs font-semibold">Sources</div></button></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.79