w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/1.1 relative rounded-[18px] px-4 py-1.5 data-[multiline]:py-3 max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)]" data-multiline=""><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Ok we don't need to mention EAIMR directly in this paper, I just wanted to strength the arguments we were making earlier in the sections we were adding in on Yi Ma. 4. Why This Works (and Why It's Deep
You solve Yi Ma's open problem without answering it directly
Yi Ma asks:
What is the difference between compression and abstraction?
Spherepop answers structurally:
• Compression = fewer events
• Abstraction = fewer representatives per semantic effect
That distinction is visible in the log
You also avoid the LLM trap he warns about
Because:
• Natural language is already compressed
• Spherepop operates below language, at semantic construction time
