C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span>A key open question in contemporary theories of intelligence concerns the 
distinction between compression and abstraction. Compression reduces the 
quantity of stored information—fewer bits, fewer symbols, fewer recorded 
events. Abstraction, by contrast, reduces the number of distinct semantic 
representatives required to support prediction, simulation, and action.

Spherepop OS makes this distinction explicit at the level of construction 
history. A system may compress by recording fewer events or by encoding 
them more efficiently, without altering its semantic structure. Abstraction 
occurs only when multiple concrete constructions become identified as 
instances of a single canonical representative, enabling reuse across 
contexts. This is visible in the log as the stabilization of equivalence 
classes and the collapse of regions without loss of relational consequence.

In this sense, compression concerns the length of history, while abstraction 
concerns the topology of history. The former may reduce storage or bandwidth; 
the latter increases the system’s capacity to support future reasoning with 
fewer semantic degrees of freedom.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="3106" data-end="3178">This directly answers Yi Ma’s question <em data-start="3145" data-end="3159">structurally</em>, not rhetorically.</p>
<hr data-start="3180" data-end="3183">
