</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Core Ontology}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

Spherepop OS is built on a minimal semantic ontology. Rather than assuming
files, processes, or memory locations as primitives, the system begins with
objects, relations, and equivalence—each defined operationally through
events.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Semantic Object]
A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{semantic object} is an abstract entity identified by a stable handle.
Objects have no intrinsic properties beyond those induced by their
participation in relations and equivalence classes.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

Objects do not exist independently of the event log. An object is said to
exist at time </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> if and only if it has been introduced by a creation event
with sequence identifier less than or equal to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Relation]
A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{relation} is a typed, directed association between two semantic
objects. Relations are first-class and may carry non-authoritative metadata.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Equivalence]
An </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{equivalence relation} over semantic objects identifies multiple
handles as representing a single canonical representative. Equivalence is
induced by merge events and maintained via a deterministic union--find
structure.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

Equivalence plays a central semantic role. Two objects that are equivalent
are interchangeable in all authoritative relations. Importantly, equivalence
is not inferred; it must be constructed explicitly via events. This
distinguishes structural abstraction from accidental similarity.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Authoritative Event Log}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

The authoritative substrate of Spherepop OS is a single append-only event
log.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{axiom}[Append-Only Authority]
All authoritative state transitions in Spherepop OS are recorded as events in
a single append-only log. No other structure is permitted to introduce,
modify, or delete semantic state.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{axiom}

Each event is assigned a strictly increasing sequence identifier by a single
arbiter, establishing a total order over all state transitions.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Deterministic State]
Given an initial empty state and a prefix of the event log, the resulting
semantic state is uniquely determined.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
The kernel applies events sequentially using deterministic transition rules.
Since the log is immutable and totally ordered, replay from the same prefix
yields the same state.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

This property elevates the event log from an implementation artifact to the
primary semantic object of the system. The log is not merely a record of
what happened; it </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{is} the system.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Events as Semantic Commitments}

Each event represents an irreversible semantic commitment. Once appended,
an event cannot be undone or modified; later events may only refine,
identify, or relate existing structure.

This irreversibility is essential. It ensures that abstraction arises
through stabilization over time rather than retroactive reinterpretation.
The system never rewrites history; it only builds upon it.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Kernel Semantics}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

The kernel of Spherepop OS is a minimal deterministic interpreter of events.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Kernel]
The </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{kernel} is the function that maps a log prefix to a semantic state
by replaying events in order. It has no hidden state and produces no side
effects beyond derived views.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

The kernel maintains derived structures such as equivalence classes and
relation tables. These structures are caches: they may be reconstructed at
any time by replay and are never authoritative.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Kernel Operations}

The kernel supports a small, closed set of event types:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{POP}: introduce a new object
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{MERGE}: induce equivalence between objects
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{LINK}: create a relation
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{UNLINK}: remove a relation
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{COLLAPSE}: bulk equivalence over a region
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{SET</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>META}: attach non-causal metadata
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

Each event type has a fixed schema and deterministic interpretation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Kernel State}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Kernel State]
A kernel state is a tuple
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> = (O, U, R, M)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a finite set of object identifiers,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U : O </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a union--find parent map,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subseteq</span></span><span> O </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> O </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a set of typed relations,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M : O </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{K} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rightharpoonup</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{V}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a partial metadata
map.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

We write </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>(o)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> for the canonical representative of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
under </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> after path compression.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Operational Semantics}

Kernel execution is defined by a labeled transition relation
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{e} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{POP}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{
  o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\notin</span></span><span> O
}{
  (O, U, R, M) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{POP}(o)}
  (O </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cup</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span>o</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> U[o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> o],</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> R,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> M)
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{MERGE}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{
  o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1, o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> O
}{
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{MERGE}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2)} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U'(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2)) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Merge Idempotence]
Applying a MERGE event to already-equivalent objects has no effect.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{LINK}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{
  (o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\notin</span></span><span> R
}{
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{LINK}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,t)}
  (O, U, R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cup</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2),t)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>, M)
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{UNLINK}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{
  (o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> R
}{
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{UNLINK}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,t)}
  (O, U, R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\setminus</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2),t)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>, M)
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{COLLAPSE}

Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subseteq</span></span><span> O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be a region and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> its representative.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{COLLAPSE}(S,o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r)} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where for all </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U'(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o)) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{rep}(o</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{SET</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>META}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{SET</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>META}(o,k,v)}
(O, U, R, M[o </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> (k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> v)])
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{axiom}[Metadata Orthogonality]
Metadata updates do not affect object existence, relations, or equivalence.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{axiom}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Semantic Properties}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Determinism]
For any kernel state </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and event </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, there exists at most one
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> such that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{e} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Confluence of Equivalence]
The equivalence relation induced by a set of MERGE events is independent of
their order.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
Union--find induces the same partition for any ordering of merges, since the
final equivalence relation is the transitive closure of the merge relation.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}
Semantic abstraction in Spherepop OS is path-independent: it depends on
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{which} identifications are made, not on </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{when} they occur.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% --- CONTINUE NEXT MESSAGE ---</span></span><span>
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="7190" data-end="7193">
<h3 data-start="7195" data-end="7222">Next message will cover</h3>
<p data-start="7223" data-end="7412"><strong data-start="7223" data-end="7278">Diffs, snapshots, replay equivalence, seekable time</strong>, and explicitly tie<br>
these to <strong data-start="7308" data-end="7352">self-consistency and simulation capacity</strong> (Yi Ma’s second<br>
principle), still without mentioning EAIMR.</p>
<p data-start="7414" data-end="7444" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Say <strong data-start="7418" data-end="7432">“continue”</strong> when ready.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 1