</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Geometry, Layout, and Gauge Freedom}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

Spherepop OS makes a strict distinction between semantic structure and
geometric presentation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Layout Hint]
A layout hint is non-causal metadata attached to an object, expressing
advisory geometric information such as position, scale, or clustering
intent.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

Layout hints may be created, modified, or discarded freely by observers and
have no effect on kernel semantics.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{axiom}[Geometric Gauge Freedom]
For any two assignments of layout hints </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, replay
of the same event log yields identical semantic state.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{axiom}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}
Geometry in Spherepop OS is a gauge choice, not a semantic constraint.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

This parallels gauge freedom in physics: multiple geometric
representations correspond to the same underlying structure.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}
Visualization layers may diverge arbitrarily without compromising semantic
correctness.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Observers and Synchronization}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Observer]
An observer is a process that receives diffs derived from kernel transitions
and maintains a local view of semantic state.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

Observers possess no authority and cannot directly modify kernel state.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{axiom}[Causal Delivery]
Observers receive diffs in strictly increasing event order.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{axiom}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Observer Convergence]
If two observers process the same diff prefix, they converge to equivalent
semantic views.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
All diffs are derived from deterministic kernel transitions applied to the
authoritative log. Since kernel transitions are pure, diff application is
order-preserving and confluent.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

Late-joining observers may receive snapshots followed by diffs, achieving
eventual consistency.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Arbiter and Collaboration Model}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Arbiter]
The arbiter is the sole authority permitted to append events to the
authoritative log.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

Clients submit proposals, which the arbiter validates and transforms into
canonical events.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{axiom}[Single Sequencer]
There exists exactly one arbiter per authoritative log.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{axiom}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Proposal Determinism]
Given identical kernel state and proposal, the arbiter produces the same
canonical event or rejection.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

This ensures global causal order while permitting decentralized
participation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Computational Complexity}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Kernel Operation Bounds]
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be the number of objects and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> the number of relations.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{POP}: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O(1)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{MERGE}: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>(n))</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> amortized
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{LINK}/</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{UNLINK}: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> m)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{COLLAPSE}: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O(|S| </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>(n))</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> for region </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Replay Complexity]
Replaying a log of length </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ell</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> requires </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ell</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>(n))</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> time.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

These bounds ensure scalability for long-lived semantic histories.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Rationale and Comparative Analysis}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

Spherepop OS differs fundamentally from existing paradigms:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Operating systems}: Unlike POSIX kernels, all state is
replayable and introspectable.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Databases}: Unlike CRDTs, Spherepop enforces a single total
order.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Version control}: Unlike Git, speculation is continuous and
first-class.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{AI systems}: Unlike language models, abstraction emerges from
construction rather than symbol compression.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

The system may therefore be understood as an operating system for semantic
time rather than hardware resources.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Conclusion}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

Spherepop OS presents a deterministic semantic operating system grounded in
causal clarity, replayability, and semantic primacy. By elevating the event
log to the sole authority and separating causes from views, the system
supports collaboration, speculation, and abstraction without sacrificing
consistency.

Crucially, Spherepop resolves foundational questions raised by Yi Ma and
others regarding compression versus abstraction. Compression is the
reduction of causal construction; abstraction is the reduction of semantic
representatives. Both are visible, measurable, and enforceable within the
log.

Spherepop OS thus occupies a pre-linguistic stratum of intelligence: a
substrate in which structure, reuse, and equivalence precede symbols. In
doing so, it offers a rigorous foundation for future systems that must
reason, collaborate, and evolve over time without losing coherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% Appendices</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ==================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\appendix</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Determinism and Confluence}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Global Determinism]
For any prefix of the authoritative log, the resulting semantic state is
unique.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
By induction on event sequence length using kernel determinism.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Compression--Abstraction Duality}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}
Compression minimizes event count; abstraction minimizes representative
count. The two quantities are independently variable.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proposition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Relation to Yi Ma's Theory}

Yi Ma characterizes intelligence as governed by parsimony and
self-consistency </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\parencite</span></span><span>{ma2023}. Spherepop OS realizes these principles
architecturally rather than heuristically.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Cybernetics Revisited}

Spherepop extends Wiener’s cybernetics by enforcing total causal order and
semantic replayability </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\parencite</span></span><span>{wiener1948}.

