t-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-2"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="229">Perfect — below is <strong data-start="19" data-end="36">MESSAGE 8 / N</strong>, adding <strong data-start="45" data-end="74">both requested extensions</strong> in a way that is fully consistent with the existing Spherepop OS manuscript, written in dense academic prose, and suitable for a long-form LuaLaTeX paper.</p>
<p data-start="231" data-end="263">Specifically, this message adds:</p>
<ul data-start="265" data-end="556">
<li data-start="265" data-end="399">
<p data-start="267" data-end="399"><strong data-start="267" data-end="304">(2) A Category-Theoretic Appendix</strong>: making the semantic kernel precise in terms of colimits, coequalizers, and functorial replay.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="400" data-end="556">
<p data-start="402" data-end="556"><strong data-start="402" data-end="434">(1) A Thermodynamic Appendix</strong>: grounding determinism, irreversibility, and abstraction in non-equilibrium statistical mechanics and entropy production.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="558" data-end="704">Nothing here mentions EAIMR explicitly. The connection to Yi Ma’s parsimony/self-consistency framework is implicit and structural, not rhetorical.</p>
<hr data-start="706" data-end="709">
<h2 data-start="711" data-end="766"><strong data-start="714" data-end="766">MESSAGE 8 / N — Category Theory + Thermodynamics</strong></h2>
