e1-a831-28b6d5f1c1de" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-2"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="365">Excellent — a companion paper is exactly the right move here.<br data-start="61" data-end="64">
What follows is <strong data-start="80" data-end="140">the start of a full, standalone LuaLaTeX companion paper</strong>, written in academic prose, explicitly engaging <strong data-start="189" data-end="243">Yi Ma’s “Mathematical Foundations of Intelligence”</strong> while positioning <strong data-start="262" data-end="278">Spherepop OS</strong> as a structural resolution of his open questions <em data-start="328" data-end="364">without importing EAIMR explicitly</em>.</p>
<p data-start="367" data-end="534">I will write this as a <strong data-start="390" data-end="428">conceptual and formal bridge paper</strong>, not a systems spec. It can be published independently or cited alongside the Spherepop OS specification.</p>
<p data-start="536" data-end="632">Below is <strong data-start="545" data-end="562">MESSAGE 1 / N</strong> of the companion paper. Subsequent messages will continue seamlessly.</p>
