<li data-start="6029" data-end="6152">
<p data-start="6032" data-end="6152"><strong data-start="6032" data-end="6069">Semantic Energy and Stabilization</strong><br data-start="6069" data-end="6072">
(why abstraction corresponds to the elimination of future causal obligations)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6154" data-end="6276">
<p data-start="6157" data-end="6276"><strong data-start="6157" data-end="6208">Why Language Is a Derived View, Not a Substrate</strong><br data-start="6208" data-end="6211">
(language as a lossy observer projection over semantic events)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6278" data-end="6399">
<p data-start="6281" data-end="6399"><strong data-start="6281" data-end="6346">Equivalence, Identity, and the Failure of Symbolic Ontologies</strong><br data-start="6346" data-end="6349">
(why identity must be event-sourced, not named)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6401" data-end="6514">
<p data-start="6404" data-end="6514"><strong data-start="6404" data-end="6455">Why This Is an Operating System and Not a Model</strong><br data-start="6455" data-end="6458">
(Spherepop vs. simulators, databases, and ML systems)</p>
</li>
