="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-2"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="155">Excellent. Below is <strong data-start="20" data-end="31">Paper B</strong>, the <strong data-start="37" data-end="68">companion theoretical paper</strong>, written as a <strong data-start="83" data-end="135">stand-alone, long-form academic LaTeX manuscript</strong>. It is designed to:</p>
<ul data-start="157" data-end="617">
<li data-start="157" data-end="279">
<p data-start="159" data-end="279">Integrate <strong data-start="169" data-end="197">abstraction as reduction</strong>, <strong data-start="199" data-end="225">memory-first reasoning</strong>, <strong data-start="227" data-end="247">replay semantics</strong>, and <strong data-start="253" data-end="279">semantic stabilization</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="280" data-end="367">
<p data-start="282" data-end="367">Align structurally with <strong data-start="306" data-end="322">Spherepop OS</strong> <em data-start="323" data-end="367">without repeating its system specification</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="368" data-end="446">
<p data-start="370" data-end="446">Address the <strong data-start="382" data-end="420">compression vs abstraction problem</strong> implicitly and rigorously</p>
</li>
<li data-start="447" data-end="522">
<p data-start="449" data-end="522">Remain <strong data-start="456" data-end="474">pre-linguistic</strong>, <strong data-start="476" data-end="495">non-LLM-centric</strong>, and <strong data-start="501" data-end="522">causally faithful</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="523" data-end="617">
<p data-start="525" data-end="617">Read as philosophy-of-computation / foundations-of-intelligence rather than OS documentation</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="619" data-end="760">No explicit references are made to Yi Ma, Chain of Memory, EAIMR, or the uploaded papers — their ideas appear as <strong data-start="732" data-end="759">structural consequences</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="762" data-end="765">
