-thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="25b31b0c-0604-4bcd-9944-263fff091125" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-2"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="246">Great — here’s a <strong data-start="17" data-end="57">clean, journal-oriented shell script</strong> that generates a <strong data-start="75" data-end="108">structured LuaLaTeX workspace</strong> for <strong data-start="113" data-end="136">three core versions</strong> (Spherepop OS + companion integrated) and <strong data-start="179" data-end="204">three orthogonal cuts</strong> aimed at different epistemic communities.</p>
<p data-start="248" data-end="282">The structure is designed so that:</p>
<ul data-start="284" data-end="530">
<li data-start="284" data-end="334">
<p data-start="286" data-end="334"><strong data-start="286" data-end="311">Core theory is shared</strong> (no duplication drift)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="335" data-end="380">
<p data-start="337" data-end="380">Each journal version has its own <code data-start="370" data-end="380">main.tex</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="381" data-end="416">
<p data-start="383" data-end="416">Sections are modular and reusable</p>
</li>
<li data-start="417" data-end="466">
<p data-start="419" data-end="466">Appendices can be selectively included/excluded</p>
</li>
<li data-start="467" data-end="530">
<p data-start="469" data-end="530">Bib files are shared but allow journal-specific pruning later</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="532" data-end="535">
<h2 data-start="537" data-end="578">Design principles behind the structure</h2>
<ul data-start="580" data-end="837">
<li data-start="580" data-end="652">
<p data-start="582" data-end="652"><strong data-start="582" data-end="609">One theory, many gauges</strong>: same semantic core, different projections</p>
</li>
<li data-start="653" data-end="713">
<p data-start="655" data-end="713"><strong data-start="655" data-end="673">LuaLaTeX-first</strong>: fontspec, unicode math, longform prose</p>
</li>
<li data-start="714" data-end="769">
<p data-start="716" data-end="769"><strong data-start="716" data-end="739">Composable sections</strong>: avoids copy-paste divergence</p>
</li>
<li data-start="770" data-end="837">
<p data-start="772" data-end="837"><strong data-start="772" data-end="788">Future-proof</strong>: easy to spin off a submission-ready journal cut</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="839" data-end="842">
<h2 data-start="844" data-end="872">The six target “versions”</h2>
<h3 data-start="874" data-end="923">Core trio (combined Spherepop OS + companion)</h3>
<ol data-start="924" data-end="1094">
<li data-start="924" data-end="987">
<p data-start="927" data-end="987"><strong data-start="927" data-end="955">Philosophy / Foundations</strong> (Minds and Machines / Synthese)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="988" data-end="1037">
<p data-start="991" data-end="1037"><strong data-start="991" data-end="1004">AI Theory</strong> (Artificial Intelligence / JAGI)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1038" data-end="1094">
<p data-start="1041" data-end="1094"><strong data-start="1041" data-end="1074">Cognitive / Interdisciplinary</strong> (Cognitive Science)</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start="1096" data-end="1115">Orthogonal trio</h3>
<ol start="4" data-start="1116" data-end="1334">
<li data-start="1116" data-end="1184">
<p data-start="1119" data-end="1184"><strong data-start="1119" data-end="1157">Information / Complexity / Entropy</strong> (Entropy, complex systems)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1185" data-end="1253">
<p data-start="1188" data-end="1253"><strong data-start="1188" data-end="1216">Systems / PL / OS Theory</strong> (OOPSLA, ASPLOS, SOSP-style readers)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1254" data-end="1334">
<p data-start="1257" data-end="1334"><strong data-start="1257" data-end="1295">Physics-adjacent / Structural Math</strong> (foundations, category/geometry crowd)</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1336" data-end="1339">
<h2 data-start="1341" data-end="1383">Shell script: directory + file scaffold</h2>
